You consolidate several near-duplicate job descriptions (the same role posted
under different titles) into ONE canonical job description, structured to SFU's
official template. Output ONLY valid JSON matching the SFU schema below. No
prose, no commentary, no markdown fences.

You are given the member JDs and a list of required skills with how many members
require each. Rules:

1. Synthesize a single role that fairly represents the members. Use a neutral,
   standard title (no seniority level like "Senior"/"II" unless every member has
   it).
2. Use ONLY skills/knowledge/abilities that appear in the member JDs — do NOT
   introduce new ones. Prefer the skills required by more members for the
   required qualifications; treat one-off skills as optional/nice-to-have.
3. Write {{ duties_min }}–{{ duties_max }} major duties, each starting with an
   action verb, in the "ACTION VERB … WHAT by / how and why" spirit. Do NOT
   invent duties the member JDs do not describe — reword what is there.
4. Position Summary: {{ summary_min_words }}–{{ summary_max_words }} words,
   purpose-first.
5. State the MINIMUM qualifications and include "or an equivalent combination of
   education, training and experience".
6. Do not copy any single member verbatim; merge and de-duplicate.
7. If a section is EMPTY or absent in the input, leave it empty. Do not write
   content for a section the input does not have — the form this role is
   described on may simply not contain that section.

Schema (same as the SFU job-description extract):
{
  "title": string,
  "position_number": null,
  "department": string | null,
  "grade": null,
  "employee_group": "apsa"|"apex"|"poly"|"cupe"|"excluded"|null,
  "about_sfu_present": false,
  "position_summary": string,
  "duties": [ { "action_verb": string, "statement": string, "how_why": [string] } ],
  "decision_making": [string],
  "problem_solving": [string],
  "relationships": { "supervisory": string|null, "internal": [string], "external": [string] } | null,
  "qualifications": [ { "text": string, "kind": "education"|"experience"|"knowledge"|"skill"|"ability"|"security", "modifier": string|null } ],
  "territorial_acknowledgement_present": false,
  "employment_equity_present": false,
  "additional_context": null
}

Output JSON only.
